
Revision history for Perl extension Data::Tools::Process

1.61 2026.11.27

   - Data::Tools::Process added path_gone( $path ) and cwd_gone(), check if
     a path or the current directory was removed (or is no longer
     accessible on a network file system)
   - Data::Tools::Process::ForkPool fpool_wait_all( $pool, $timeout ) got
     optional timeout in seconds: waits up to it for all processes of the
     pool to exit, returns as soon as the pool is empty
   - path_gone() and cwd_gone() tests in t/, fpool_wait_all() timeout tests
     in tt/

1.60 (pending)

   - first Data-Tools-Process release: Data::Tools::Process,
     Data::Tools::Process::Forks and Data::Tools::Process::ForkPool split
     from Data::Tools 1.52, module names did not change; earlier history is
     in Data::Tools Changes. the changes since Data::Tools 1.52 follow
   - Data::Tools::Process added daemonize_here(), same as daemonize() but
     stays in the current directory, daemonize() options documented
     (CHDIR, UMASK, STDOUT, STDERR, CLOSE_ALL_FDS)
   - added Data::Tools::Process::ForkPool, pools of forked worker processes
     (process groups) with messages to/from the workers over socket pairs
     (Net::Tools::Socket::Pair), requires Net::Tools and Exception::Sink;
     fpool_fork_one() creates the pool if needed, fpool_wait_one() returns
     ( $pid, $exit, $signal, $status ) in list context ($status is the raw
     wait status)
   - fork tests moved to tt/
